data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgrades the underlying library from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1. Key breaking changes:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.OpenApiString` | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `schema.Example = JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — use `schema.Type` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` | `new OpenApiReference("oauth2", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = scopes }` | Use `Schemes` dictionary property |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString removed; use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiReference now takes constructor args
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement no longer inherits from Dictionary;
    // use the Schemes property instead
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property removed in v3.1 model;
                // remove Null from the Type flags instead
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of fixes:**
1. Replace `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` with `using System.Text.Json.Nodes`
2. `new OpenApiString("1.0")` → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")`
3. `new OpenApiReference { Type = ..., Id = ... }` → `new OpenApiReference("oauth2", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)`
4. `new() { [scheme] = scopes }` → create instance, then `requirement.Schemes.Add(...)`
5. `.Nullable = false` → clear the `Null` flag: `.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`
